>and one more thing, S_NYMPH was my first idea and it doesnt work,

Yes it does!! But you should have specified SPFX_DCLAS for your
artifact instead of SPFX_DFLAG2.

Observe the artilist.h definitions of Dragonbane and Trollsbane
(artifacts targeting a monster class), and compare them to Werebane and
Demonbane (artifacts targeting monster types).

Also: you need to specify SPFX_RESTR as well, or otherwise the player
can create the artifact by #naming a sword.

>next: let the altar stay, but i will use some penalties, like an altar
>is created for 1 turn only, and you cant pray to often, can you?

Firstly: you could just  create an altar immediately upon entering
Astral and thus bypass an important part of the endgame.
Secondly, how do you intend to destroy the altar, anyway? What if the
player level-teleports immediately after creating it?
Thirdly, why do you even want altar creation in the first place?

>and why do you say not to use autoredobjnam?

WELL, all it does is call readobjnam(<your string>, &zeroobj, TRUE).
What's the point?

And, you seem to be using it to create an altar using an ability of
readobjnam() which, among other things, only works in Wizard mode. If
you want to make an altar at the player's position, do this:

levl[u.ux][u.uy].altarmask = Align2amask( <your alignment> );
newsym(u.ux, u.uy);

